When producing the shipped copies, JuicyLucy excludes tests and evals,
redirects hyperframes-cli's render-approval reference to video-ad-production's gate policy,
replaces hyperframes-animation's instructions to install the third-party
`animate-text` skill with its own build-from-description fallback,
replaces unversioned `npx hyperframes` invocations with `hyperframes` so
the installed, pinned CLI is used, points command invocations of the
installed tools at their launchers under `~/.juicylucy/bin`, replaces
hyperframes-cli's upgrade instructions with the plugin's pinned-CLI rule, and rewrites the folded multi-line
`description` of hyperframes-audio, hyperframes-cli and hyperframes-keyframes
as one quoted line with the same words, and removes the upstream-only
`metadata: internal: true` flag from the frontmatter of captions-overlay,
cut-the-curve, motion-doctrine, oversized-cursor and seam-craft. It also
leaves out media-use's own audio engine with its third-party voice, music and
sound-effect provider integrations and bundled sound effects, and
hyperframes-cli's hosted cloud-rendering reference, and rewrites the lines
that pointed at them. These are JuicyLucy's distribution changes.
Each modified upstream file also carries a prominent modification notice.
The pinned commit is recorded in
vendor/hyperframes/UPSTREAM.lock in the source repository; the build checks
that this NOTICE names the same commit. The Apache licence applies to those
eleven skills only, not to the rest of this product.
